      role: 'Buffers the controller port lines onto the data bus. U19 reads port 1, U18 reads port 2.', pkg: 'DIP-20',
      machines: ['colecovision'], location: { colecovision: 'U18, U19' },
      summary: 'Two 3-state octal buffers put the controller lines on the data bus when a game reads $FC (port 1, U19) or $FF (port 2, U18). The strobes that pick joystick or keypad come from U24 (74LS00 latch), not from these chips. The Technical Manual\'s check: with nothing pressed, inputs (U18 pins 3-9, U19 pins 2-8) below 2.2 V mean a bad buffer. Its troubleshooting chart also names U24 and U6 for controller faults.',
